<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">Limb VII &middot; i &mdash; a sub-limb of God, the Law of One &amp; the Contact Question</p>
  <h1>The Law of One</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">A channeled cosmology dictated, it claims, by a sixth-density intelligence called Ra
  and taken down over three years in a Louisville living room. This order reads it more closely than any
  other modern revelation &mdash; not as scripture, but as philosophy, and as the single most internally
  coherent document of its kind.</p>
</section>

<!-- ============================ THE POSITION ============================ -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">The Order's Position <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
    <h2 id="t-shelved-without-embarrassment">Shelved, Without Embarrassment</h2>
    <p class="lede">Let us say plainly what this page is and is not. The <em>Law of One</em> makes claims
    about the structure of reality that cannot be tested and are not, by any stretch, established. We shelve
    it with the <span class="myth">vision</span> mark and do not pretend otherwise.</p>
    <p>What earns it a room of its own is different. Across five books and some two thousand questions, the
    material holds a single metaphysics with almost no self-contradiction: one Creator knowing itself through
    its parts, a ladder of densities climbed by the discipline of love or the discipline of wisdom, free will
    so sacred that even the highest intelligences refuse to break it. It declines the falsifiable predictions
    its imitators trade on. And it closes nearly every session by telling the reader to keep only what
    resonates and discard the rest &mdash; an extraordinary posture for a text that could easily demand
    obedience.</p>
    <p>We read it, then, as a serious work of esoteric philosophy and as a primary document of the
    twentieth-century contact imagination &mdash; the way one reads the <em>Corpus Hermeticum</em> or the
    Neoplatonists. Not because it is proven. Because it is <em>thought through</em>, and thinking is the
    subject of this order.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">&#10022;</div>

<!-- ============================ WHAT IT IS ============================ -->
<section class="wrap reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">Begin Here <span class="hist">&#9670;</span></p>
    <h2 id="t-what-the-material-is">What the Material Actually Is</h2>
    <p class="lede">Before the cosmology, the record &mdash; because the record is a matter of history, and
    history can be checked.</p>
    <p><strong>The circle.</strong> <span class="hist">&#9670;</span> The material comes from
    <em>L/L Research</em>, a small group in Louisville, Kentucky: <strong>Don Elkins</strong>, a former
    physics professor and airline pilot who had spent two decades investigating the paranormal;
    <strong>Carla Rueckert</strong>, the instrument; and later <strong>Jim McCarty</strong>, who joined as
    scribe and editor. From 1981 until Elkins's death in 1984 &mdash; and in a longer second arc from 1981
    through the 1990s &mdash; the group held sittings in which Rueckert entered a trance, and an intelligence
    identifying itself as <em>Ra</em> answered questions put to it.</p>
    <p><strong>The method.</strong> <span class="hist">&#9670;</span> This was not automatic writing or a
    Ouija board. Elkins (and later McCarty) asked prepared questions aloud; Rueckert, in trance, spoke the
    answers in a flat, formal, deliberately archaic register; McCarty took them down. The sessions were tape
    recorded and transcribed. Rueckert reported no memory of the content while tranced. Whatever one makes of
    it, the <em>process</em> is documented in extraordinary detail &mdash; the group published the raw
    transcripts, its own doubts, and even the "instrument's" physical cost.</p>
    <p><strong>The voice.</strong> <span class="myth">&#9670;</span> Ra describes itself as a
    <em>social memory complex</em> of the sixth density &mdash; not a single being but a merged, collective
    consciousness &mdash; and claims two prior contacts with Earth: among the Atlanteans some eleven thousand
    years ago, and in Egypt around the reign of Akhenaten, the pharaoh who briefly turned his kingdom toward
    the worship of one god, the sun-disc Aten. Ra says both contacts were, in its telling, failures &mdash;
    the message of unity was distorted into hierarchy and empire. It is a striking admission for a revelatory
    text to make about itself.</p>
    <p class="muted small">The five books &mdash; <em>The Law of One</em>, Books I&ndash;V &mdash; were
    published between 1982 and 1998 and remain in print, freely distributed by L/L Research. The material
    seeded much of what is now called New Age vocabulary: the "densities," "wanderers," "service to others,"
    "harvest."</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">&#10022;</div>

<!-- ============================ THE PLATES ============================ -->
<section class="wrap reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">Eight Plates</p>
    <h2 id="t-the-architecture">The Architecture of the Teaching</h2>
    <p class="lede">The whole system turns on one sentence and its consequences. Here is the sentence, then
    the machinery built from it.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid two">

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate I <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>The Law Itself: All Is One</h3>
      <p>The first and governing claim. There is no separation. Every person, stone, star and galaxy is a
      distortion &mdash; a local inflection &mdash; of a single infinite Creator. "All things are one. There
      is no wrong way. There is no polarity." Evil and good, self and other, are not ultimate; they are
      surface ripples on one substance that has chosen, in order to know itself, to appear as many.</p>
      <p>This is not a fuzzy sentiment in the material; it is the axiom everything else is derived from, the
      way a geometry is derived from its postulates.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate II <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>Intelligent Infinity and the Distortions</h3>
      <p>The source Ra calls <em>intelligent infinity</em> &mdash; undifferentiated, infinite, conscious,
      without parts. It cannot be described, only approached through its <em>distortions</em>, the successive
      "bendings" by which the One becomes a universe.</p>
      <p>The first distortion is <strong>free will</strong> &mdash; the Creator's decision to allow itself to
      be surprised. The second is the <em>Logos</em>, creative love or light, the shaping principle. The third
      is light itself. From these the whole cosmos unfolds, and free will &mdash; being first &mdash; outranks
      everything, including truth and even love. This is why non-interference is absolute in the material.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate III <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>The Densities</h3>
      <p>Existence is not flat. It is a ladder of seven <em>densities</em> &mdash; octaves of being &mdash;
      with an eighth that begins the next octave, as the eighth note of a scale begins the next scale:</p>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><strong>First</strong> &mdash; earth, water, air, fire: the awareness of <em>being</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Second</strong> &mdash; plant and animal: growth, movement, the awareness of <em>other</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Third</strong> &mdash; self-consciousness: the density of <em>choice</em>. This is humanity's present station, and the only one where the great choice is made.</li>
        <li><strong>Fourth</strong> &mdash; love and understanding.</li>
        <li><strong>Fifth</strong> &mdash; wisdom and light.</li>
        <li><strong>Sixth</strong> &mdash; the balance of love and wisdom into unity. Ra's own density.</li>
        <li><strong>Seventh</strong> &mdash; the gateway, the completion of the octave, where the soul turns back toward the source.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted small">Each density has its "lesson," and a being advances only by mastering it &mdash;
      there is no skipping.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate IV <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>The Veil of Forgetting</h3>
      <p>Why would a being choose to be born blind to its own divinity? The material's answer is its most
      elegant move. In third density a <em>veil</em> is drawn: the soul forgets that it is the Creator, forgets
      its past lives, forgets that its enemy is itself. Only against that forgetting can a choice be genuine.
      A being that <em>knew</em> it was one with all could not truly choose to serve or to seize; the answer
      would be given, not earned.</p>
      <p>The veil makes love possible by making love <em>risky</em>. Suffering, on this account, is not
      punishment but <em>catalyst</em> &mdash; the friction against which polarization happens.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate V <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>Service to Others and Service to Self</h3>
      <p>The great choice of third density is a polarization, and the material is radical in insisting that
      <em>both</em> poles are legitimate. One may climb by <strong>service to others</strong> &mdash; the
      positive path, the way of love &mdash; or by <strong>service to self</strong> &mdash; the negative path,
      the way of separation, domination and control. Neither is forbidden. Both are coherent. Both are
      climbed.</p>
      <p>The asymmetry is not moral but structural. The negative path, Ra says, is ultimately entropic: a
      being wholly turned inward eventually consumes everything it can dominate and is left alone with itself,
      which is a kind of death. The positive path compounds. The material never calls the negative path
      <em>wrong</em> &mdash; only, in the end, a dead end of its own logic.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate VI <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>The Harvest</h3>
      <p>Third density runs in great cycles &mdash; a major cycle of roughly 75,000 years &mdash; at whose end
      comes the <em>harvest</em> or <em>graduation</em>. Each soul is weighed, not by deeds tallied but by its
      <em>polarization</em>: the degree to which it has oriented toward others or toward self.</p>
      <p>The thresholds are the material's most quoted figures. To graduate to the positive fourth density a
      soul must be at least <strong>51% service to others</strong>. To graduate to the negative fourth Density
      it must be at least <strong>95% service to self</strong> &mdash; a far harder mark, which is one way the
      text encodes its claim that selfishness is the narrower door. Souls that reach neither repeat third
      density. There is no eternal hell here; there is only more time, and another choice.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate VII <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>Wanderers and the Social Memory Complex</h3>
      <p>Two ideas do a great deal of work in the material. A <em>wanderer</em> is a being from a higher
      density &mdash; fourth, fifth, sixth &mdash; who voluntarily incarnates into the heaviness and the veil
      of third density in order to serve, risking a kind of amnesia and, Ra says, real danger of getting
      caught in the karma it came to lighten. Wanderers are the material's saints and bodhisattvas.</p>
      <p>A <em>social memory complex</em> is what a group becomes at the upper densities: not a hive that
      erases the individual, but a communion in which every member's experience is available to all and the
      group mind is richer than any part. Ra is one. It is the material's picture of heaven &mdash; not a
      place but a <em>way of being together</em>.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate VIII <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>The Confederation and the Orion Group</h3>
      <p>The cosmos is populated by intelligences, grouped by their polarization. The
      <em>Confederation of Planets in the Service of the Infinite Creator</em> &mdash; some fifty-three
      civilizations, of which Ra is one &mdash; serves. The <em>Orion group</em> seeks to conquer and enslave.
      Both are bound by the first distortion: neither may violate free will. So the Confederation answers only
      when called and gives no proof that would compel belief, while Orion works by temptation and the
      exploitation of those already turned toward self.</p>
      <p class="muted small">This is the material's theodicy: the "negative" is permitted, even useful, as the
      resistance that makes the positive choice mean something. It is also why Ra will not simply prove itself
      &mdash; proof would collapse the veil and void the choice.</p>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

