<!-- ============================ THE LEDGER ============================ -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2 id="t-what-survives">What Survives Scrutiny</h2>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="hist">&#9670;</span> The material exists, is documented, and its process is unusually transparent &mdash; tapes, transcripts, published doubts.</li>
        <li><span class="hist">&#9670;</span> It is internally coherent across five books and some two thousand questions &mdash; rare for a channeled text.</li>
        <li><span class="hist">&#9670;</span> It demonstrably seeded modern New Age vocabulary: the densities, wanderers, service-to-others, the harvest.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> Its ethics &mdash; non-interference, service to others, the refusal to compel belief &mdash; are philosophically serious and worth engaging on their merits.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> Read as a modern theodicy, the "evil as permitted catalyst" move is coherent and has real antecedents in Irenaeus and in process thought.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> As a primary document of the twentieth-century contact imagination, it is genuinely valuable &mdash; a window onto what the century longed for.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2>What Does Not</h2>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> <strong>That Ra is a sixth-density intelligence.</strong> Untestable, and the trance channel that produced it is fully explicable as a dissociative or imaginative state of a gifted instrument.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> <strong>The densities, the harvest, the 75,000-year cycles.</strong> No independent evidence; the numbers are asserted, not derived, and no prediction has been confirmed.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> <strong>The Atlantis and Akhenaten contacts.</strong> Atlantis is not an archaeological reality, and the Aten cult is thoroughly documented without any need of extraterrestrial advice.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> <strong>Wanderers among us.</strong> A claim that cannot be distinguished from the ordinary fact that some people are unusually kind or unusually cruel.</li>
        <li><span class="hist">&#9670;</span> <strong>That it is unique.</strong> Its cosmology is a synthesis &mdash; Neoplatonist emanation, Theosophical root-races and rounds, Vedantic non-dualism, and the channeled idiom of its own decade. Knowing the sources makes it richer, not poorer.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted small mt-1">As ever, discarding the unsupportable strengthens the serious residue. The
      material does not need Ra to be real in order to be worth reading; it needs only to be thought through,
      and it is.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ THE TIMELINE ============================ -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">Lineage</p>
    <h2 id="t-a-record">A Record of the Material</h2>
    <ul class="timeline">
      <li><strong>1950s&ndash;60s</strong> &mdash; Don Elkins, a physicist, spends two decades investigating UFO contactees, hypnotic regression and the paranormal, growing steadily more sceptical of the sensational and more interested in the consistent.</li>
      <li><strong>1970s</strong> &mdash; Elkins and Carla Rueckert develop the trance method; early "personality" contacts give way to something the pair take more seriously.</li>
      <li><strong>1981</strong> &mdash; The Ra sessions begin in earnest. The intelligence gives its name and its cosmology; Jim McCarty joins as scribe.</li>
      <li><strong>1982</strong> &mdash; <em>The Law of One, Book I</em> is published.</li>
      <li><strong>1984</strong> &mdash; Books II and III appear; Don Elkins dies, and the first arc of the material closes with him.</li>
      <li><strong>1986&ndash;1998</strong> &mdash; A second, longer series of sittings produces Books IV and V; L/L Research continues to publish and to distribute the transcripts freely.</li>
      <li><strong>1990s&ndash;present</strong> &mdash; The vocabulary escapes into the wider culture: "wanderer," "density," "service to others." The material becomes a reference point &mdash; argued with, borrowed from, and rarely read in full.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ GLOSSARY + READING ============================ -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2>Glossary</h2>
      <dl class="glossary">
        <dt>Intelligent infinity</dt>
        <dd>The undifferentiated, infinite, conscious source; the One before it bends into a universe.</dd>
        <dt>Distortion</dt>
        <dd>A "bending" of the One into a particular thing. Free will is the first distortion; everything real is one.</dd>
        <dt>Density</dt>
        <dd>An octave of being, from mineral (first) to the gateway (seventh), climbed by mastering each one's lesson.</dd>
        <dt>The veil</dt>
        <dd>Third density's forgetting, drawn so that the choice to serve or to seize can be genuine.</dd>
        <dt>Polarization</dt>
        <dd>The degree to which a soul has turned toward others or toward self; the measure by which it is harvested.</dd>
        <dt>Harvest</dt>
        <dd>The graduation at a cycle's end: 51% service-to-others for the positive fourth density, 95% service-to-self for the negative.</dd>
        <dt>Wanderer</dt>
        <dd>A higher-density soul incarnated into third density to serve, at the risk of the veil and of karma.</dd>
        <dt>Social memory complex</dt>
        <dd>A group mind in which every member's experience is shared; what Ra is, and the material's picture of heaven.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2 id="t-reading">Reading</h2>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="hist">&#9670;</span> <strong>The Law of One, Books I&ndash;V</strong> (L/L Research, 1982&ndash;1998) &mdash; the primary material, distributed free by the circle that took it down.</li>
        <li><span class="hist">&#9670;</span> <strong>Carla L. Rueckert, <em>What Love Is</em></strong> and her other writings &mdash; the instrument's own, untranced voice, and a useful corrective to reading Ra as scripture.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> <strong>Hans Baer &amp; colleagues, on the New Age milieu</strong> &mdash; for placing the material in the twentieth-century esoteric revival it both drew on and fed.</li>
        <li><span class="hist">&#9670;</span> <strong>The <em>Corpus Hermeticum</em> and Plotinus</strong> &mdash; the emanation cosmology the densities quietly rhyme with.</li>
        <li><span class="hist">&#9670;</span> <strong>Shankara's <em>Vivekachudamani</em></strong> &mdash; non-dualism proper, against which the Law of One's monism can be measured.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> <strong>Jane Roberts, the Seth Material</strong> and <em>A Course in Miracles</em> &mdash; the material's closest kin in the channeled idiom of its decade.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ WHERE WE STAND ============================ -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">The Closing Stance</p>
    <h2 id="t-where-this-order-stands">Where This Order Stands</h2>
    <p class="lede">We do not believe Ra is waiting on the other side of a trance in Kentucky. We are not
    convinced by the densities, the harvest, or the arithmetic of salvation, and this page has said so in the
    ledger without flinching.</p>
    <p>And yet we give the material a room of its own, because it does something few revelations manage: it
    thinks. It takes one axiom &mdash; that all is one &mdash; and follows it, honestly and without special
    pleading, into cosmology, ethics, suffering and death. It refuses to compel belief. It blesses the freedom
    of the being who would seize as readily as the being who would serve, and then shows, without rage, why
    seizing is a corridor with no door at the end. It tells the reader, again and again, to keep only what
    rings true.</p>
    <p>A text that confident in its own thinking has nothing to fear from ours. Read it as the modern esoteric
    document it is: shelved <span class="myth">&#9670;</span>, deliberately and without embarrassment, beside
    the Hermetica and the Upanishads, and worth every hour spent arguing with it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

